\paragraph{Unified Regime Taxonomy Across Campaign Space.}
Figure~\ref{fig:regime_map_z0m_ug} consolidates the field observations into a single roughness-forcing phase diagram $(z_{0m}, U_g)$. High-roughness and strong-forcing regimes support continuous weak turbulence (Regime I), low-roughness and weak-forcing combinations induce runaway radiative decoupling (Regime III), and the intermediate corridor supports self-sustained relaxation oscillations (Regime II). Overlaying CASES-99, FLOSS, and SHEBA demonstrates that these campaigns represent distinct operating points on a single unified dynamical manifold.

